1
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:12,179
<i>It was a desolate wasteland,
consumed by the darkness of night.</i>

2
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:17,810
<i>Over many moons, the people labored
to make the land habitable.</i>

3
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:21,604
<i>Eventually, vegetation burst into life,</i>

4
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:23,356
<i>the crops thrived,</i>

5
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:25,234
{\an8}<i>and a country was born.</i>

6
00:00:26,402 --> 00:00:30,364
{\an8}<i>It was a country of peace and prosperity,
but it all changed one year.</i>

7
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>Spring never arrived,</i>

8
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:36,537
<i>and the harsh winter cold
showed no signs of relenting.</i>

9
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:41,417
<i>As the land froze,
the people could do nothing but tremble.</i>

10
00:00:44,712 --> 00:00:47,715
{\an8}<i>One man had vanished from the country,</i>

11
00:00:49,216 --> 00:00:51,761
<i>and his disappearance
was the catalyst for this change.</i>

12
00:00:53,763 --> 00:00:57,849
<i>His absence triggered
all manner of anomalies,</i>

13
00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:00,852
<i>anomalies that changed
the very fabric of nature.</i>

14
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:04,899
<i>And then, 20 years passed.</i>

15
00:02:36,031 --> 00:02:39,952
THE MESSAGE

16
00:02:42,496 --> 00:02:46,458
<i>The spirits had agreed on a deadline:
Walpurgis Eve.</i>

17
00:02:47,585 --> 00:02:52,381
<i>That fateful morning had arrived
in the Country of Long Nights.</i>

18
00:02:58,512 --> 00:03:00,346
Oh, my, My Lady.

19
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:02,808
You could have stayed in bed longer.

20
00:03:03,309 --> 00:03:05,101
No way I could.

21
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:07,062
Can I wash my face?

22
00:03:08,063 --> 00:03:10,148
I'll have your outfit
from yesterday laundered.

23
00:03:10,149 --> 00:03:13,109
You'll be out in town today,
so please dress like a lady.

24
00:03:13,110 --> 00:03:15,570
May I let your hair down?

25
00:03:15,571 --> 00:03:17,781
Whatever. I don't care.

26
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:27,750
Oh, my, who might that be?

27
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:35,214
The prince consort has something
he'd like to return to Miss Eleonora.

28
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:38,886
As such, Her Majesty
requests her company for breakfast.

29
00:03:40,179 --> 00:03:41,305
<i>The queen?</i>

30
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:45,350
Many great lords
and members of the royal family

31
00:03:45,351 --> 00:03:48,603
come from lineages of priestesses
and shamans who could hear

32
00:03:48,604 --> 00:03:50,981
the voices of nature
and spirits in ancient times.

33
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:54,443
Maid.

34
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,654
I'll go, so get things ready.

35
00:04:00,324 --> 00:04:03,077
What? Ellie went to see the queen?

36
00:04:03,661 --> 00:04:06,829
Yes. I just hope it helps her
get a little more accustomed

37
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:09,208
to dining with foreign dignitaries.

38
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:10,834
Is that so?

39
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:13,336
Was Ellie mad at me?

40
00:04:13,337 --> 00:04:15,380
She's not at all angry!

41
00:04:15,381 --> 00:04:17,966
What are you talking about?

42
00:04:17,967 --> 00:04:21,552
Well, it was so cold
that I crawled into the covers on my own,

43
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:23,179
so perhaps it was a bit cramped.

44
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,932
I received a massive scolding for it
once, long ago.

45
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:28,811
That's quite the story
first thing in the morning.

46
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:36,777
<i>I was told breakfast
would be served in the basement.</i>

47
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:41,698
I hope you didn't get lost, Miss Eleonora.

48
00:04:41,699 --> 00:04:43,033
This way, please.

49
00:04:43,701 --> 00:04:46,077
Let's hurry up and finish breakfast.

50
00:04:46,078 --> 00:04:49,956
The spring festival starts today,
so we'll be going around town.

51
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:51,332
Speaking of the festival,

52
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:54,420
apparently, this country has more spirits
now than at any other time.

53
00:04:55,421 --> 00:04:57,964
Flowers bloom and crops
ripen all at once in spring,

54
00:04:57,965 --> 00:05:00,426
drawing spirits both good
and evil to the land.

55
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:01,760
Flowers...

56
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,724
Apparently,
it isn't entirely superstition.

57
00:05:07,850 --> 00:05:11,019
The direct royal line is especially
susceptible to spirit possession,

58
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:14,647
so no major affairs of state
are decided during this period.

59
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,024
That's what I heard.

60
00:05:16,025 --> 00:05:18,402
And you would be entirely correct.

61
00:05:19,153 --> 00:05:23,157
However, it seems spirits have
a hard time approaching the church,

62
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:26,618
so during this period,
the church takes the royals' place

63
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:29,329
and accepts inquiries
and requests for help.

64
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:32,915
So, the archbishop?

65
00:05:32,916 --> 00:05:36,711
I hope you'll come to me
in your times of need.

66
00:05:36,712 --> 00:05:40,757
Is that because the church
is a sacred place?

67
00:05:40,758 --> 00:05:44,010
No, it seems the spirits
don't like hot springs.

68
00:05:44,011 --> 00:05:44,845
Hot springs?

69
00:05:45,763 --> 00:05:48,807
You know how that place has
a water clock and other water features?

70
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:00,652
Is this place...

71
00:06:06,784 --> 00:06:09,577
Have you taken a dip
in the hot springs here yet?

72
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:10,412
Yeah.

73
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:14,540
But it was dark,
so I couldn't see a thing.

74
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:16,877
To think it's this bright
under the castle by day.

75
00:06:17,461 --> 00:06:20,339
It is. Many people
come down here during the day.

76
00:06:20,923 --> 00:06:23,132
The castle is truly beautiful.

77
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:25,259
We're stuck indoors in the winter,

78
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,346
so we get particular about our interiors.

79
00:06:29,348 --> 00:06:30,389
Her Majesty,

80
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:33,392
having breakfast in a place like that...

81
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:36,813
We can't get close to hot springs
because they cause root rot.

82
00:06:36,814 --> 00:06:38,190
What do we do now?

83
00:06:38,774 --> 00:06:41,150
She visited the church the other day.

84
00:06:41,151 --> 00:06:43,654
I wonder what she talked
to the archbishop about.

85
00:06:44,321 --> 00:06:48,032
She asked him to ensure
the Knight Commander goes home on time,

86
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,200
no matter what!

87
00:06:49,201 --> 00:06:50,701
Kastehelmi!

88
00:06:50,702 --> 00:06:52,954
The church's decisions are absolute.

89
00:06:52,955 --> 00:06:55,706
I know you were whispering
to Her Majesty in her dreams

90
00:06:55,707 --> 00:06:58,209
to get her to keep
the Knight Commander here.

91
00:06:58,210 --> 00:07:01,796
But it didn't go as planned
because the castellan of Marronnier

92
00:07:01,797 --> 00:07:04,174
sent the Knight Commander's fiancée
with him, right?

93
00:07:04,925 --> 00:07:08,886
Even if he is the Night,
he was born in a foreign land.

94
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:11,890
We mustn't burden him
with our country's problems.

95
00:07:17,604 --> 00:07:18,897
Have a seat here.

96
00:07:20,649 --> 00:07:21,984
Is it good?

97
00:07:23,986 --> 00:07:25,611
I want more.

98
00:07:25,612 --> 00:07:28,866
<i>He really is the prince consort?</i>

99
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:31,701
Oh, dear.

100
00:07:31,702 --> 00:07:35,330
My, my. Anni, Father, have some tea.

101
00:07:37,207 --> 00:07:40,294
I hear the flower spirits
caused you some trouble last night.

102
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:42,504
Not at all.

103
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:47,425
Please accept my sincere apologies,
Miss Eleonora.

104
00:07:47,426 --> 00:07:49,469
We owe an apology
to the Knight Commander, too.

105
00:07:50,095 --> 00:07:51,805
They're not bad kids.

106
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:58,561
We of the royal line
can communicate with them,

107
00:07:58,562 --> 00:08:01,481
but failed to keep them in check,
and for that, we are deeply sorry.

108
00:08:02,316 --> 00:08:05,235
I've left the rest to the church.

109
00:08:05,736 --> 00:08:07,612
Please complete your remaining duties

110
00:08:07,613 --> 00:08:09,198
and depart as planned.

111
00:08:11,074 --> 00:08:12,783
Thank you kindly.

112
00:08:12,784 --> 00:08:16,163
However, I heard that you wish to keep
the Knight Commander here, as well.

113
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:21,000
That can wait for another time.

114
00:08:21,001 --> 00:08:26,214
Should the Knight Commander
visit our country again in the spring,

115
00:08:26,215 --> 00:08:31,385
we hope he gets the chance to meet
one of his father's old friends.

116
00:08:31,386 --> 00:08:35,306
<i>Insomniac's father... Peregrinus?</i>

117
00:08:35,307 --> 00:08:36,933
<i>An old friend?</i>

118
00:08:36,934 --> 00:08:39,101
Yes, that's right.

119
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:40,896
That can wait for another time.

120
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:42,939
Is something the matter?

121
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,148
Take a look.

122
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:48,278
There are clouds in the sky
we don't usually see in the morning.

123
00:08:54,618 --> 00:08:55,826
What's up?

124
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:56,995
Nothing.

125
00:08:58,205 --> 00:09:00,958
<i>Here comes that chill again.</i>

126
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:05,378
You've been restless
ever since you woke up this year.

127
00:09:05,379 --> 00:09:06,421
What's the matter?

128
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:11,093
Why are you going to such lengths
to keep Night here?

129
00:09:19,601 --> 00:09:22,437
An outfit from the Country of Cold?
Who are you?

130
00:09:24,273 --> 00:09:27,234
What do you want?
I believe we still have time left.

131
00:09:27,943 --> 00:09:29,695
But things aren't working out, are they?

132
00:09:31,071 --> 00:09:33,739
You needn't worry.
By the time Walpurgis Eve rolls around,

133
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,657
Night will be ours.

134
00:09:34,658 --> 00:09:37,119
What are you all talking about?

135
00:09:37,703 --> 00:09:40,414
I made a promise. To these kids.

136
00:09:42,332 --> 00:09:47,754
<i>It happened on the night
Insomniac's party arrived at the castle.</i>

137
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:50,256
Who are you?

138
00:09:50,257 --> 00:09:52,466
Why ask us to make such a promise?

139
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:54,051
Because I want to...

140
00:09:54,052 --> 00:09:57,096
No, because I have to.

141
00:09:57,097 --> 00:09:58,681
In this country,

142
00:09:58,682 --> 00:10:00,892
this is probably the easiest way.

143
00:10:07,316 --> 00:10:10,234
It's just like 20 years ago...

144
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:11,945
Stop! Please stop this at once!

145
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:17,117
I trust that you will do as I asked.

146
00:10:17,826 --> 00:10:21,245
We are to take the Night
to the world Saint Walpurga resides in.

147
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:23,581
By the night the spring festival begins...

148
00:10:23,582 --> 00:10:25,834
In other words, by Walpurgis Eve.

149
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:28,503
If we do, you won't start any trouble.

150
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:30,797
Do we have your word?

151
00:10:31,465 --> 00:10:32,341
Of course.

152
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:36,470
Fine. We'll do it.

153
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:39,681
It's a promise, then.

154
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:58,575
That's why we tried to keep
the Night from leaving this country.

155
00:10:59,242 --> 00:11:00,868
I see...

156
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:03,913
I'm tired of waiting,
so I'll take it from here.

157
00:11:03,914 --> 00:11:04,748
Kastehelmi!

158
00:11:05,791 --> 00:11:06,625
What?

159
00:11:07,751 --> 00:11:09,002
Your Majesty!

160
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:10,878
What's the matter?

161
00:11:10,879 --> 00:11:11,963
Take Kastehelmi!

162
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,134
No way!

163
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:21,972
Kastehelmi! Help her, now!

164
00:11:21,973 --> 00:11:24,017
Will someone check
what's happening up there?

165
00:11:24,726 --> 00:11:25,894
Oh?

166
00:11:27,646 --> 00:11:29,147
Buying time, are we?

167
00:11:34,111 --> 00:11:37,489
Forget all that.
Let's make it Walpurgis Eve already.

168
00:11:49,751 --> 00:11:52,045
<i>Time advanced in an instant,</i>

169
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:57,259
<i>and the Country of Long Nights
ushered in Walpurgis Eve.</i>

170
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:01,012
The sky...

171
00:12:02,764 --> 00:12:05,934
What the... The sun only just came up!

172
00:12:13,483 --> 00:12:16,652
Archbishop! The festival's bonfire has...

173
00:12:16,653 --> 00:12:19,281
What in the world?

174
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:24,326
What is happening?

175
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:27,205
I've never seen anything like it.

176
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,667
Morning suddenly turned to night.

177
00:12:31,835 --> 00:12:33,420
What could it mean?

178
00:12:39,050 --> 00:12:40,384
Why?

179
00:12:40,385 --> 00:12:41,844
What's going on?

180
00:12:41,845 --> 00:12:43,388
Is he a monster?

181
00:12:45,015 --> 00:12:46,558
He's a monster!

182
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:49,853
I need the Night to take my place.

183
00:12:50,812 --> 00:12:53,190
Before Walpurgis Eve ends.

184
00:12:53,815 --> 00:12:55,150
I must hurry.

185
00:12:56,902 --> 00:12:59,196
Are you all right, Kastehelmi?

186
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:02,239
I'm fine.

187
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,700
How could they do this to her?

188
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:07,077
The spirits made a bold choice.

189
00:13:07,078 --> 00:13:08,121
What happened?

190
00:13:10,248 --> 00:13:13,585
Someone that wasn't a spirit
suddenly appeared up there.

191
00:13:14,461 --> 00:13:17,087
He threatened the spirits

192
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:21,467
into taking the Night to Saint Walpurga.

193
00:13:21,468 --> 00:13:25,263
If they did that,
he said he wouldn't harm our country.

194
00:13:26,139 --> 00:13:28,140
- Take Kastehelmi upstairs.
- At once.

195
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:31,228
Father, do you know what's happening?

196
00:13:32,354 --> 00:13:34,021
It's hard to say.

197
00:13:34,022 --> 00:13:36,274
We don't have enough information.

198
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:41,028
If the Knight Commander is the target,

199
00:13:41,029 --> 00:13:43,030
may I go take a look at him?

200
00:13:43,031 --> 00:13:44,907
Did you say something?

201
00:13:44,908 --> 00:13:46,660
Nothing, my dear.

202
00:13:47,244 --> 00:13:48,702
Listen up.

203
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:51,581
Evacuate our guests
to the inner chambers on the first floor.

204
00:13:52,082 --> 00:13:54,542
The royal guard will follow
Captain Mika's orders.

205
00:13:54,543 --> 00:13:55,377
Yes, My Lady!

206
00:14:03,301 --> 00:14:04,427
Old-timer.

207
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:07,096
Can you tell who he is
just by looking at him?

208
00:14:07,097 --> 00:14:09,640
I can. I am a scholar, you know.

209
00:14:09,641 --> 00:14:11,351
You, for example...

210
00:14:11,935 --> 00:14:13,686
How should I put this?

211
00:14:13,687 --> 00:14:14,813
You need...

212
00:14:15,814 --> 00:14:18,525
to grow up a little more.

213
00:14:21,403 --> 00:14:23,822
You still have time, but you must hurry.

214
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:34,416
So, what kind of information
are you looking for?

215
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,709
A name, to begin with.

216
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,711
As long as I have a name,

217
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:40,462
I can find out where he was born

218
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:43,091
and perhaps even his ancestors' names.

219
00:14:45,969 --> 00:14:48,304
This castle's pretty big.

220
00:14:48,305 --> 00:14:50,265
Now, where could the Night be?

221
00:14:51,683 --> 00:14:53,934
There's been an emergency.

222
00:14:53,935 --> 00:14:57,605
We must ask you to evacuate
to the inner chambers on the first floor.

223
00:14:57,606 --> 00:15:00,358
What is going on, Captain?

224
00:15:00,942 --> 00:15:04,696
An enemy with unknown powers
has appeared near the castle walls.

225
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:07,824
Is this enemy the one
who turned morning to night?

226
00:15:08,408 --> 00:15:10,577
It's likely. He's by himself.

227
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:13,038
And his target is the Knight Commander.

228
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:25,091
Strange. His power seems dispersed.

229
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:29,053
I don't want to tire myself out here.

230
00:15:29,054 --> 00:15:32,724
In that case, make sure you're completely
exhausted before you reach the castle!

231
00:15:36,102 --> 00:15:36,978
Everyone!

232
00:15:44,486 --> 00:15:47,364
<i>But this power won't be a burden.</i>

233
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:55,038
Please report to Her Majesty.

234
00:16:06,508 --> 00:16:10,052
Is it this country's spirits
that are fighting the enemy right now?

235
00:16:10,053 --> 00:16:10,969
That's right.

236
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:13,098
Now, hurry to safety.

237
00:16:16,059 --> 00:16:20,145
<i>I have to hide from someone who can turn
morning to night in the blink of an eye?</i>

238
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:22,023
<i>Isn't that impossible?</i>

239
00:16:23,108 --> 00:16:24,275
<i>Then I might as well...</i>

240
00:16:25,485 --> 00:16:27,070
In that case, Knight Commander,

241
00:16:29,239 --> 00:16:32,033
will you fight him alongside us?

242
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:33,575
That's reckless!

243
00:16:33,576 --> 00:16:35,744
If you'll let me.

244
00:16:35,745 --> 00:16:39,665
Facing him myself may limit the damage.

245
00:16:39,666 --> 00:16:40,500
Hey...

246
00:16:42,544 --> 00:16:44,462
Johann, make the preparations.

247
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:48,466
Lord Ambassador, please ask Eleonora
to intercept the enemy.

248
00:16:49,592 --> 00:16:50,802
There you are!

249
00:16:54,514 --> 00:16:56,098
I'm sorry, Lord Ambassador.

250
00:16:56,099 --> 00:16:58,809
What's the matter, Insomniac?

251
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:00,729
Pass on a message to Ellie for me.

252
00:17:07,444 --> 00:17:08,402
Maid.

253
00:17:08,403 --> 00:17:11,906
My Lady! Why are you eating cake
without a worry in the world?

254
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:15,451
It's times like these
that you need to fill your belly.

255
00:17:15,452 --> 00:17:18,830
I understand that,
but people usually lose their appetite.

256
00:17:19,456 --> 00:17:20,415
Where's Insomniac?

257
00:17:21,082 --> 00:17:24,168
He headed to his room after breakfast.

258
00:17:24,169 --> 00:17:25,879
He should be here soon.

259
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:30,341
I'd like to have a nice, long chat
with you once we're back.

260
00:17:31,426 --> 00:17:34,137
<i>We can go home, right, Insomniac?</i>

261
00:17:47,275 --> 00:17:49,401
Hey, what's going on?

262
00:17:49,402 --> 00:17:51,696
Don't ask me. I have no idea.

263
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:57,410
Did he turn morning to night
so he could use his powers to the fullest?

264
00:17:57,994 --> 00:17:59,912
If so, he must be...

265
00:17:59,913 --> 00:18:03,332
He must be what other lands call
a monster from the world's end.

266
00:18:03,333 --> 00:18:05,376
What should we do?

267
00:18:06,419 --> 00:18:08,296
We must hold out a little longer.

268
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,340
Your Majesty, let's surrender
to the Night!

269
00:18:11,341 --> 00:18:13,134
Before he rains down hail!

270
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:18,223
<i>It must be because
the Knight Commander came to our castle.</i>

271
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:24,478
I can tell, I feel so much better
after a good night's sleep.

272
00:18:24,479 --> 00:18:26,814
The chancellor's secret message said

273
00:18:26,815 --> 00:18:30,068
the Knight Commander would bring
wealth and prosperity to our country.

274
00:18:30,735 --> 00:18:34,781
But the king and the castellan
are too humane to want him to stay.

275
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:39,743
Perhaps the balance of powers
shifted somehow.

276
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:43,998
The influence of the spirits on you
is stronger than usual this year.

277
00:18:44,707 --> 00:18:47,042
Let's stick to the original plan

278
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:50,546
and bring the Knight Commander and her
together at the church

279
00:18:50,547 --> 00:18:52,340
as the ceremony's main event.

280
00:18:53,967 --> 00:18:56,094
Just picture it, Hyrrokkin.

281
00:18:56,594 --> 00:19:00,389
If you departed to Marronnier
and didn't return,

282
00:19:00,390 --> 00:19:03,934
then even if I were told
I'd die tomorrow if I didn't stay in bed,

283
00:19:03,935 --> 00:19:05,770
I'd still go search for you.

284
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:10,774
That's not special or anything.

285
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:13,903
It's just what anyone
in that position would do.

286
00:19:23,204 --> 00:19:26,748
I see. There are as many of you
as there are flowers.

287
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:30,628
You're no dry grass,
so you won't burn easily.

288
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,768
Fall back, everyone.

289
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:47,645
Now.

290
00:19:49,022 --> 00:19:50,815
I'll waltz in through the front door.

291
00:20:00,325 --> 00:20:02,951
You all did very well.

292
00:20:02,952 --> 00:20:05,496
Was this the right thing to do,
Your Majesty?

293
00:20:06,247 --> 00:20:08,458
Will our country be all right?

294
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,169
You needn't worry.

295
00:20:11,669 --> 00:20:13,962
Even if assailed by a hailstorm,

296
00:20:13,963 --> 00:20:18,550
we've spent millennia
making these frozen lands our home,

297
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:19,928
have we not?

298
00:20:27,143 --> 00:20:28,353
Eleonora.

299
00:20:28,937 --> 00:20:30,646
Get ready and go upstairs.

300
00:20:30,647 --> 00:20:32,731
Insomniac and Johann are waiting

301
00:20:32,732 --> 00:20:34,359
in the second-floor hallway.

302
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:36,986
Then I don't have to wear this anymore?

303
00:20:37,487 --> 00:20:38,987
Is my gear ready, maid?

304
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:43,117
Yes. It's in the room next door.
I'll have it ready right away.

305
00:20:43,701 --> 00:20:45,661
A report from Her Majesty.

306
00:20:45,662 --> 00:20:47,621
The enemy is a young man.

307
00:20:47,622 --> 00:20:52,126
So far, we've confirmed that he can use
flame, ice, and water magic.

308
00:20:52,669 --> 00:20:54,962
<i>Flame, ice, and...</i>

309
00:20:54,963 --> 00:20:55,797
<i>Ellie.</i>

310
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:59,634
I put a spell on it
for some extra peace of mind.

311
00:21:02,053 --> 00:21:03,929
Take care of Insomniac for us.

312
00:21:03,930 --> 00:21:05,515
We're counting on you, Ellie.

313
00:21:10,645 --> 00:21:12,730
<i>I appreciate the peace of mind.</i>

314
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:17,318
Please don't push yourself too hard.

315
00:21:18,152 --> 00:21:18,987
I'll be off, then.

316
00:21:19,737 --> 00:21:21,488
What's the enemy's maximum range?

317
00:21:21,489 --> 00:21:24,574
We've confirmed a range
of about eight meters.

318
00:21:24,575 --> 00:21:25,951
Where's Mika's squad?

319
00:21:25,952 --> 00:21:28,328
In the hallway with the Knight Commander,

320
00:21:28,329 --> 00:21:30,664
by the castle gates, and around the plaza.

321
00:21:30,665 --> 00:21:34,419
Then split into two and head for
the castle gates and the plaza.

322
00:21:35,837 --> 00:21:38,839
- I'll head to the hallway.
- Ma'am!

323
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,132
Eleonora.

324
00:21:40,133 --> 00:21:43,886
I have a message from Insomniac for you.

325
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,681
Don't worry about it.

326
00:21:47,682 --> 00:21:51,185
Even I can do up
her sleeve buttons for her.

327
00:22:17,754 --> 00:22:19,130
<i>Insomniac...</i>

328
00:22:19,672 --> 00:22:22,007
<i>I still don't really get it,</i>

329
00:22:22,008 --> 00:22:23,718
<i>but you have this side to you...</i>

330
00:22:24,302 --> 00:22:26,095
<i>You say these things I don't understand.</i>

331
00:22:26,679 --> 00:22:30,391
<i>I don't know how the castellan
explained it to you.</i>

332
00:22:31,184 --> 00:22:32,685
<i>But I'm on my way now.</i>

333
00:22:33,936 --> 00:22:36,147
<i>Make sure to explain it
so I can understand.</i>

334
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:42,070
<i>Everyone in the castle says the castellan
saddled me with you, but...</i>

335
00:22:44,864 --> 00:22:46,907
Everyone, get away from here!

336
00:22:46,908 --> 00:22:48,117
Insomniac!

337
00:22:48,618 --> 00:22:51,119
<i>But in my eyes,
what I've been saddled with</i>

338
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,247
<i>is the castellan's job
and the land, not you.</i>

339
00:23:05,426 --> 00:23:06,844
What was that?

340
00:23:13,267 --> 00:23:14,310
Insomniac?

341
00:24:48,279 --> 00:24:50,697
{\an8}<i>The Night isn't human.</i>

342
00:24:50,698 --> 00:24:52,365
{\an8}<i>He won't die from this, right?</i>

343
00:24:52,366 --> 00:24:56,120
{\an8}<i>Don't talk about him like you know him!</i>

344
00:24:58,789 --> 00:25:00,958
MY NAME'S NOT INSOMNIAC FOR NOTHING

345
00:25:03,961 --> 00:25:05,963
Subtitle translation by: Sriram Gurunathan

